269
00:09:53,760 --> 00:09:55,130
-Follow me out, then.

270
00:09:55,130 --> 00:09:55,890
-Follow you?

271
00:09:55,890 --> 00:09:56,390
-Sex appeal.

272
00:09:56,390 --> 00:09:58,790
-Listen, I can change clothes
 and beat you out there.

273
00:09:58,790 --> 00:10:02,090
-[LAUGHING]

274
00:10:02,090 --> 00:10:05,000
-Again, sorry about the face!

275
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:06,210
-That's my girl.

276
00:10:06,210 --> 00:10:07,610
Her father's Robert I. Miller.

277
00:10:07,610 --> 00:10:09,370
-Yeah, just pump
 my gas, butthead.

278
00:10:09,370 --> 00:10:11,420
-I saw this venture boat.

279
00:10:11,420 --> 00:10:13,850
You oughta see her swim.

280
00:10:13,850 --> 00:10:14,350
-Hey!

281
00:10:14,350 --> 00:10:15,550
-You're putting
 that in the wayback!

282
00:10:15,550 --> 00:10:18,140
My kids are back there!

283
00:10:18,140 --> 00:10:20,770
-I don't know why, but I
 wish he'd pistol whip him.

284
00:10:20,770 --> 00:10:22,840
-Gee, I sure am sorry, sir.

285
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:24,550
-But I'm sort of an idiot.

286
00:10:24,550 --> 00:10:27,160
-Guess I was thinking about
 having dinner with my girl.

287
00:10:27,160 --> 00:10:28,290
She lives up at the club.

288
00:10:28,290 --> 00:10:30,790
-Yeah, with Robert I. Miller.

289
00:10:30,790 --> 00:10:35,710
-(SINGING) 77 Sunset Strip.

290
00:10:35,710 --> 00:10:40,410
-(SINGING) How will you
 make it on your own?

291
00:10:40,410 --> 00:10:44,590
-[HONKING] I've got a
 new swimsuit, everybody!

292
00:10:44,590 --> 00:10:45,290
-Oh no!

293
00:10:45,290 --> 00:10:46,650
She's chasing down Emmett Kelly!

294
00:10:49,230 --> 00:10:51,670
-Suddenly, she began to
 doubt the whole bathing suit

295
00:10:51,670 --> 00:10:54,460
purchase.

296
00:10:54,460 --> 00:10:55,920
-Eegah!

297
00:10:55,920 --> 00:10:59,810
-[SCREAMING]

298
00:10:59,810 --> 00:11:00,430
-Whoa.

299
00:11:00,430 --> 00:11:00,930
-My fault.

300
00:11:00,930 --> 00:11:01,660
Sorry.

301
00:11:01,660 --> 00:11:04,800
All my fault.

302
00:11:04,800 --> 00:11:05,490
-I'm with Allstate.

303
00:11:05,490 --> 00:11:08,510
Who are you with?

304
00:11:08,510 --> 00:11:10,890
-[SPEAKING_GERMAN]

305
00:11:10,890 --> 00:11:13,970
-[GROANING]

306
00:11:13,970 --> 00:11:15,320
-[SPEAKING_CAVEMAN]

307
00:11:15,320 --> 00:11:16,890
-Which way to bly workshop?

308
00:11:16,890 --> 00:11:18,690
-[SPEAKING_CAVEMAN]

309
00:11:18,690 --> 00:11:20,040
-[CLEARS_THROAT]

310
00:11:20,040 --> 00:11:21,950
-[SPEAKING_CAVEMAN]

311
00:11:21,950 --> 00:11:26,790
-You know, I heard Kiel
 ad-libbed this entire scene.

312
00:11:26,790 --> 00:11:27,290
-Hey, funny.

313
00:11:27,290 --> 00:11:28,560
I was driving a
 stick, too. [LAUGHING]

314
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:30,550
-[SPEAKING_CAVEMAN]

315
00:11:30,550 --> 00:11:34,340
-Ugh, damn foreign cars.

316
00:11:34,340 --> 00:11:36,790
-Well, there's something
 you don't see every day.

317
00:11:42,210 --> 00:11:43,110
-It's the hose clamp.

318
00:11:43,110 --> 00:11:44,280
Uh, you'll want to
 get that checked

319
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:46,840
when you get back to town.

320
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:48,310
-[GRUNT]

321
00:11:48,310 --> 00:11:49,260
-Oh, forget it.

322
00:11:49,260 --> 00:11:51,630
I'm going back to
 sleep. [SNORING]

323
00:11:51,630 --> 00:11:54,040
-Uh, found this in your grill.

324
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:56,070
Probably what was
 causing all the trouble.

325
00:11:56,070 --> 00:11:59,360
-[SPEAKING_CAVEMAN]

326
00:11:59,360 --> 00:12:04,240
-So, uh, you had a root beer
 and a side of fries with that?

327
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:05,210
-Mm, nah.

328
00:12:05,210 --> 00:12:06,600
Eegah can't go with that.

329
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:07,830
Not much leg room.

330
00:12:07,830 --> 00:12:09,610
Huh-uh.

331
00:12:09,610 --> 00:12:13,180
-Say, could you give me a lift
 to Stephen J. Gould's house?

332
00:12:13,180 --> 00:12:15,040
-[SPEAKING_CAVEMAN].

333
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:16,630
-Jim Morrison, the Paris years.

334
00:12:19,170 --> 00:12:22,260
-Oh, he's doing Tai Chi on her.

335
00:12:22,260 --> 00:12:23,200
[HONKING]

336
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:25,080
-[YELLS]

337
00:12:25,080 --> 00:12:29,790
-[SPEAKING_CAVEMAN]

338
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:30,780
-[SCREAMING]

339
00:12:30,780 --> 00:12:32,020
-I'm still making payments!

340
00:12:32,020 --> 00:12:34,860
-Busted!

341
00:12:34,860 --> 00:12:37,610
-Saved by the Vette.

342
00:12:37,610 --> 00:12:38,110
-Hey, Eegah!

343
00:12:38,110 --> 00:12:38,810
How you doing, buddy?

344
00:12:45,810 --> 00:12:47,500
-[SCREAMING]

345
00:12:47,500 --> 00:12:48,000
-Roxy!

346
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,040
It's me, Tom!

347
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:50,930
-That's why I'm
 screaming! [SCREAM]

348
00:12:50,930 --> 00:12:52,830
-Oh, Tommy!

349
00:12:52,830 --> 00:12:53,790
-What's the matter?

350
00:12:53,790 --> 00:12:54,570
What happened?

351
00:12:54,570 --> 00:12:56,660
-There was a Poco
 song on the radio.

352
00:12:56,660 --> 00:12:58,020
-Oh, is he gone?

353
00:12:58,020 --> 00:12:59,370
-Who?

354
00:12:59,370 --> 00:12:59,990
-Is he?

355
00:12:59,990 --> 00:13:00,490
-Disney?

356
00:13:00,490 --> 00:13:01,460
-Huh?

357
00:13:01,460 --> 00:13:04,400
-I don't see anybody.

358
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:07,960
Just take it easy and
 tell me what happened.

359
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:11,090
-Uh, is she really
 going out with him?

360
00:13:11,090 --> 00:13:13,000
-I did!

361
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:16,830
Honest, I saw a giant!

362
00:13:16,830 --> 00:13:18,030
-Ooh, that face.

363
00:13:18,030 --> 00:13:19,390
I feel handsome in comparison.

364
00:13:19,390 --> 00:13:21,160
-You know, the nice
 thing about this car

365
00:13:21,160 --> 00:13:22,870
is that she can fold it up
 and put it in her purse.

366
00:13:22,870 --> 00:13:23,640
-It's a compact.

367
00:13:23,640 --> 00:13:26,280
-Yeah.

368
00:13:26,280 --> 00:13:27,870
-Crate and Barrel?

369
00:13:27,870 --> 00:13:30,520
-Hey?

370
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:33,260
-No, it was right in
 the middle of the road.

371
00:13:33,260 --> 00:13:35,570
Not a half a mile from here.

372
00:13:35,570 --> 00:13:36,760
-William Faulkner!

373
00:13:36,760 --> 00:13:39,140
-He doesn't believe me.

374
00:13:39,140 --> 00:13:43,650
-You didn't really expect
 anyone to, did you, Miss Miller?

375
00:13:43,650 --> 00:13:44,250
-Why not?

376
00:13:44,250 --> 00:13:45,090
It's the truth.

377
00:13:45,090 --> 00:13:46,660
-Ooh, good comeback.

378
00:13:46,660 --> 00:13:49,040
-Honey, a, uh,
 prehistoric monster

379
00:13:49,040 --> 00:13:51,540
is a rather large
 order to swallow.

380
00:13:51,540 --> 00:13:53,360
-Dad, I didn't say
 he was a monster.

381
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:55,370
He was a giant.

382
00:13:55,370 --> 00:13:56,220
-It's a big difference.

383
00:13:56,220 --> 00:13:58,540
-You know, a caveman.

384
00:13:58,540 --> 00:14:00,250
Club and all, eh?

385
00:14:00,250 --> 00:14:00,930
-Yes.

386
00:14:00,930 --> 00:14:03,220
-What my daughter saw, she saw.

387
00:14:03,220 --> 00:14:05,490
Now let's just
 let it go at that.

388
00:14:05,490 --> 00:14:07,120
-Could you just take
 our order, please?

389
00:14:07,120 --> 00:14:09,400
-Well, if you see
 your giant again,

390
00:14:09,400 --> 00:14:12,160
let me know in time
 to take some pictures?

391
00:14:12,160 --> 00:14:15,400
-Come to Eegah Retirement
 Village, for the good life.

392
00:14:15,400 --> 00:14:18,440
-Town caves and slag heaps
 starting at $100,000.

393
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:19,900
-Couldn't you have
 imagined the whole thing?

394
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:21,110
-No.

395
00:14:21,110 --> 00:14:23,320
-Now, let's be
 realistic about this.

396
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:25,090
You said yourself
 that you fainted.

397
00:14:25,090 --> 00:14:28,880
Isn't it possible that you
 dreamed this whole idea?

398
00:14:28,880 --> 00:14:29,400
-No, Dad.

399
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:29,900
I didn't.

400
00:14:29,900 --> 00:14:31,010
There was a giant.

401
00:14:31,010 --> 00:14:31,940
-Oh, she's got a neat shape.

402
00:14:31,940 --> 00:14:33,680
-Now, I don't want
 to call this story

403
00:14:33,680 --> 00:14:36,960
of yours a lot of foolishness,
 and I haven't so far, have I?

404
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:37,770
-No.

405
00:14:37,770 --> 00:14:41,110
-But if there were a giant, if
 anyone at all had been here--

406
00:14:41,110 --> 00:14:41,610
-Mr. Miller!

407
00:14:41,610 --> 00:14:43,340
Come here!

408
00:14:43,340 --> 00:14:44,790
-My neck snapped!

409
00:14:44,790 --> 00:14:46,470
-What did you find?

410
00:14:46,470 --> 00:14:47,200
-I don't know.

411
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:48,680
It sure looks like
 a footprint, though.

412
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:50,230
-Let me see.

413
00:14:50,230 --> 00:14:51,110
-It's dirt!

414
00:14:51,110 --> 00:14:52,050
-Yes, look.

415
00:14:52,050 --> 00:14:54,350
There's the heel,
 and there's the toes.

416
00:14:54,350 --> 00:14:56,070
-That's an ant
 colony, you idiot!

417
00:15:00,640 --> 00:15:02,640
-Look at the size of him.

418
00:15:02,640 --> 00:15:06,240
-Glen was 50 feet tall.

419
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:08,160
-It must have been made by a--

420
00:15:08,160 --> 00:15:09,600
-Say it.

421
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:11,040
-A giant.

422
00:15:11,040 --> 00:15:12,300
-What did I tell you?

423
00:15:12,300 --> 00:15:14,940
-Hooray, I won!

424
00:15:14,940 --> 00:15:17,300
-And that's for finding it.

425
00:15:17,300 --> 00:15:20,750
-I'll find the big boy himself
 for you, if you feel like that.

426
00:15:20,750 --> 00:15:23,110
-He left the road right here.

427
00:15:23,110 --> 00:15:24,190
-Watch out for snakes.

428
00:15:24,190 --> 00:15:24,730
-Who said that?

429
00:15:27,320 --> 00:15:32,300
-Uh, let's not forget
 where we parked Super Car.

430
00:15:32,300 --> 00:15:34,280
-Better go back to the car.

431
00:15:34,280 --> 00:15:34,780
-No!

432
00:15:34,780 --> 00:15:37,440
He's my giant.

433
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:40,170
-Holy cow, he was standing
 right here watching us.

434
00:15:40,170 --> 00:15:43,140
-Playing bass.

435
00:15:43,140 --> 00:15:47,180
-Then he turned
 and took off for--

436
00:15:47,180 --> 00:15:47,680
-There?

437
00:15:50,260 --> 00:15:51,970
-Shadow Mountain.

438
00:15:51,970 --> 00:15:54,170
Do you suppose that's
 where he lives?

439
00:15:54,170 --> 00:15:57,030
-(SINGING) Oh, to live
 on Shadow Mountain.

440
00:15:57,030 --> 00:15:59,720
-That would account for his
 never having been seen before.

441
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:01,220
-It's too bad we didn't
 bring the dune buggy.

442
00:16:01,220 --> 00:16:02,660
We could go after him.

443
00:16:02,660 --> 00:16:03,930
-What for?

444
00:16:03,930 --> 00:16:05,410
-Well, to get some pictures.

445
00:16:05,410 --> 00:16:07,400
Maybe even to bring him back.

446
00:16:07,400 --> 00:16:09,780
A lot of people aren't going
 to believe this giant jazz.

447
00:16:09,780 --> 00:16:10,280
-No.

448
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:12,280
We're not to say anything
 about this, you understand?

449
00:16:12,280 --> 00:16:13,280
-Why not?

450
00:16:13,280 --> 00:16:16,260
After the way everyone
 laughed at me.

451
00:16:16,260 --> 00:16:17,320
-Your turn will come.

452
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:18,550
-He's got third degree burns!

453
00:16:18,550 --> 00:16:20,230
-Third degree sideburns.

454
00:16:20,230 --> 00:16:23,790
-Are you gonna write a book
 about giant, Mr. Miller?

455
00:16:23,790 --> 00:16:25,150
-That's the idea, Tommy.

456
00:16:25,150 --> 00:16:26,330
-I'll take you up there.

457
00:16:26,330 --> 00:16:27,920
My dune buggy's all ready to go.

458
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:28,760
-No thanks.

459
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:29,260
-It is!

460
00:16:29,260 --> 00:16:30,140
I just gave it the works!

461
00:16:30,140 --> 00:16:31,310
-There's no offense, son.

462
00:16:31,310 --> 00:16:32,400
-Dammit, son.

463
00:16:32,400 --> 00:16:34,160
-But I'd like to take
 this trip in something

464
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:35,310
a little bit safer.

465
00:16:35,310 --> 00:16:36,220
-More stylish.

466
00:16:36,220 --> 00:16:39,250
-(CRYING) He resents
 my dune buggy!

467
00:16:39,250 --> 00:16:40,390
-Watch out for snakes.

468
00:16:45,270 --> 00:16:46,070
-Whirlybirds!

469
00:16:46,070 --> 00:16:47,320
-Blue Thunder! !

470
00:16:47,320 --> 00:16:47,820
-MASH!

471
00:16:47,820 --> 00:16:48,770
-Apocalypse Now!

472
00:16:48,770 --> 00:16:49,620
-Dispatches!

473
00:16:49,620 --> 00:16:50,850
-Because, you see,
 it's a helicopter.

474
00:16:50,850 --> 00:16:52,130
-[LAUGHS] And all
 of those elements.

475
00:16:55,270 --> 00:16:59,200
-It looks like I got
 a flat tire here.

476
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:01,660
-I'll see you in about
 two days at the most.

477
00:17:01,660 --> 00:17:04,600
-Oh, please take
 care of yourself.

478
00:17:04,600 --> 00:17:06,730
-Now, my credit cards
 are in the desk drawer.

479
00:17:06,730 --> 00:17:08,600
You make sure you
 leave them there.

480
00:17:08,600 --> 00:17:10,310
-Dad's fun.

481
00:17:10,310 --> 00:17:12,460
-This thing's supposed to
 be safer than my dune buggy?

482
00:17:12,460 --> 00:17:14,780
-Oh, shut up about your dune
 buggy, you little twerp.

483
00:17:17,920 --> 00:17:18,870
-I like them.

484
00:17:18,870 --> 00:17:21,230
Yeah.

485
00:17:21,230 --> 00:17:23,990
-Uh, got my shoe trees in here.

486
00:17:23,990 --> 00:17:24,490
-Ouch!

487
00:17:24,490 --> 00:17:25,200
My hand!

488
00:17:25,200 --> 00:17:28,690
[SCREAMING AND CHOPPING NOISES]

489
00:17:38,690 --> 00:17:40,570
-Richard Nixon leaving
 the White House.

490
00:17:43,730 --> 00:17:48,170
[HUMMING_THE_"MASH"_THEME]

491
00:17:48,170 --> 00:17:50,410
-I thought we promised
 never to do that again.

492
00:17:50,410 --> 00:17:51,010
-Oh, sorry.

493
00:17:51,010 --> 00:17:51,510
-Oh.

494
00:17:51,510 --> 00:17:52,940
I had my fingers crossed.

495
00:17:52,940 --> 00:17:53,910
-Look at those legs.

496
00:18:03,850 --> 00:18:05,990
-Boy, they're really
 hitting it off.

497
00:18:16,780 --> 00:18:18,500
-Hey, Skipper, look at
 this thing on my leg here.

498
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:20,220
It's like a mole, but
 it keeps flaking off.

499
00:18:20,220 --> 00:18:22,600
See that?

500
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:24,950
-I want that!

501
00:18:24,950 --> 00:18:27,450
-Now, there should be
 a Ram Charger up there.

502
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:33,660
-Oh, for a shoulder
 mounted anti-aircraft gun.

503
00:18:33,660 --> 00:18:34,970
-Oh, you mean a stinger.

504
00:18:34,970 --> 00:18:35,470
-Whatever.

505
00:18:43,740 --> 00:18:46,640
-Commute to work or play in
 your own personal helicopter.

506
00:18:46,640 --> 00:18:50,000
Miracle Acrylic Bubble
 makes it possible.

507
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,380
-Eegah drives a tank?

508
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:00,820
-Well, uh, I don't really
 know what to say, Roy.

509
00:19:00,820 --> 00:19:03,060
Look, this isn't
 good bye, really.

510
00:19:03,060 --> 00:19:06,330
There are other
 helicopter rides.

511
00:19:06,330 --> 00:19:08,510
-So, you got everything?

512
00:19:08,510 --> 00:19:09,770
-(SPANISH ACCENT) Surprise.

513
00:19:09,770 --> 00:19:11,340
I am Jose Greco.

514
00:19:11,340 --> 00:19:12,450
-Now, don't you forget.

515
00:19:12,450 --> 00:19:15,760
I want you to meet me at the
 mouth of Deep Canyon tomorrow

516
00:19:15,760 --> 00:19:16,810
at 4:00.

517
00:19:16,810 --> 00:19:17,910
-(LAUGHING) Sure.

518
00:19:17,910 --> 00:19:18,550
4:00.

519
00:19:18,550 --> 00:19:19,050
Whatever.

520
00:19:23,670 --> 00:19:25,710
-Sure hope it doesn't get hot.

521
00:19:29,190 --> 00:19:31,370
-Jeez, that helicopter
 took off fast.

522
00:19:31,370 --> 00:19:32,310
Where'd he go?

523
00:19:35,620 --> 00:19:36,600
-Hey, to the left.

524
00:19:36,600 --> 00:19:37,480
That-- yeah.

525
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:37,980
Yeah.

526
00:19:37,980 --> 00:19:38,480
There.

527
00:19:43,100 --> 00:19:44,720
-Hey, that's my daughter!

528
00:19:44,720 --> 00:19:45,890
-See, those are
 his contact lenses.

529
00:19:45,890 --> 00:19:47,660
He's quite
 nearsighted, actually.

530
00:19:50,380 --> 00:19:52,970
-Meet him at Deep Mouth
 Canyon tomorrow at 4:00.

531
00:19:52,970 --> 00:19:54,860
What the hell was I thinking?

532
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:55,920
Jeez.

533
00:19:55,920 --> 00:19:56,440
-Oh, yeah.

534
00:19:56,440 --> 00:19:58,050
You can tell he's an
 experienced mountaineer.

535
00:20:03,150 --> 00:20:03,990
-The hell?

536
00:20:03,990 --> 00:20:05,240
