-Don't make me think so much.

805
00:30:59,690 --> 00:31:01,920
-I know, but he should
 have made it before dark.

806
00:31:01,920 --> 00:31:03,550
-Don't worry about it.

807
00:31:03,550 --> 00:31:06,430
He'll see the campfire and come
 walking in on us any minute

808
00:31:06,430 --> 00:31:06,930
now.

809
00:31:06,930 --> 00:31:08,990
-That's what you
 said two hours ago.

810
00:31:08,990 --> 00:31:11,140
-Well, he will.

811
00:31:11,140 --> 00:31:12,430
-Well, if you
 believe that, what's

812
00:31:12,430 --> 00:31:14,390
the idea with the bed roll?

813
00:31:14,390 --> 00:31:16,530
-Look, I carry all
 this junk in the buggy

814
00:31:16,530 --> 00:31:18,480
anyway, so you might as
 well get some use out of it.

815
00:31:18,480 --> 00:31:19,790
-I'm not sleepy.

816
00:31:19,790 --> 00:31:20,540
-I'm petulant.

817
00:31:20,540 --> 00:31:22,970
-When Edward Albee
 dabbles in beach movies.

818
00:31:22,970 --> 00:31:23,520
-Lie down.

819
00:31:23,520 --> 00:31:24,510
Take a rest for a while.

820
00:31:24,510 --> 00:31:25,630
I'll keep the fire going.

821
00:31:25,630 --> 00:31:30,860
-I'll just break off a pound of
 my hair at a time and burn it.

822
00:31:30,860 --> 00:31:32,610
-Hey, what are you
 doing with that?

823
00:31:32,610 --> 00:31:33,280
-[MIMICS_GUNSHOT]

824
00:31:33,280 --> 00:31:34,520
-I always carry a
 gun in the desert.

825
00:31:34,520 --> 00:31:36,580
There's coyotes around the camp.

826
00:31:36,580 --> 00:31:37,360
-Put it away.

827
00:31:37,360 --> 00:31:38,520
We're not playing cowboy.

828
00:31:38,520 --> 00:31:41,130
-You know, there's mountain
 lions around here, too.

829
00:31:41,130 --> 00:31:42,130
-And elephants and stuff.

830
00:31:42,130 --> 00:31:43,300
-Well, they won't
 come near a fire.

831
00:31:43,300 --> 00:31:43,920
I know that much.

832
00:31:43,920 --> 00:31:45,890
And I'm not going to have you
 take a shot at something that

833
00:31:45,890 --> 00:31:47,160
turns out to be dad.

834
00:31:47,160 --> 00:31:48,090
-OK, OK.

835
00:31:48,090 --> 00:31:49,280
I'll put it away
 on one condition.

836
00:31:49,280 --> 00:31:50,770
That you crawl in
 and get some rests.

837
00:31:50,770 --> 00:31:51,270
-OK.

838
00:31:51,270 --> 00:31:52,930
-I won't shoot your dad, OK?

839
00:31:52,930 --> 00:31:53,430
Jeez.

840
00:31:58,280 --> 00:31:59,570
-Uh, Roxy?

841
00:31:59,570 --> 00:32:03,470
I'm gonna sing myself to sleep.

842
00:32:03,470 --> 00:32:06,420
-He borrowed that top
 from Audrey Hepburn.

843
00:32:06,420 --> 00:32:07,710
[MUSIC PLAYING]

844
00:32:07,710 --> 00:32:08,440
-Arch, no.

845
00:32:08,440 --> 00:32:09,090
No, Arch.

846
00:32:09,090 --> 00:32:10,390
No, please.

847
00:32:10,390 --> 00:32:10,890
No.

848
00:32:10,890 --> 00:32:12,510
Please.

849
00:32:12,510 --> 00:32:14,940
-She's packed to move and can
 be drop shipped to your home

850
00:32:14,940 --> 00:32:17,340
overnight.

851
00:32:17,340 --> 00:32:21,110
-Fortunately, he remembered
 to bring the Isley Brothers.

852
00:32:21,110 --> 00:32:25,750
-It's kind of like a Mitty
 Silverton working there, huh?

853
00:32:25,750 --> 00:32:28,260
-Went on to do music
 for Sergio Leone.

854
00:32:28,260 --> 00:32:31,140
-[WHISTLING]

855
00:32:31,140 --> 00:32:33,320
-I'm Death, and I
 have visited upon you.

856
00:32:33,320 --> 00:32:37,680
-(SINGING) If I had
 1,000 paintings.

857
00:32:37,680 --> 00:32:39,620
-Well, you don't.

858
00:32:39,620 --> 00:32:41,970
-(SINGING) In a marble gallery.

859
00:32:41,970 --> 00:32:45,050
-This should keep
 the wolves away.

860
00:32:45,050 --> 00:32:47,330
-I'd be in the
 Museum of Modern Art.

861
00:32:47,330 --> 00:32:51,350
-[HUMMING] What
 the hell was that?

862
00:32:51,350 --> 00:32:54,780
-[SINGING]

863
00:32:54,780 --> 00:32:55,680
-Hey, stop smiling.

864
00:32:55,680 --> 00:32:58,000
He's smiling!

865
00:32:58,000 --> 00:32:58,880
-That's nice.

866
00:32:58,880 --> 00:33:00,680
Honey, where's your 12 gauge?

867
00:33:00,680 --> 00:33:10,170
-[SINGING]

868
00:33:10,170 --> 00:33:11,240
-I've heard enough.

869
00:33:11,240 --> 00:33:12,420
I'll go beat him senseless.

870
00:33:12,420 --> 00:33:15,700
-[SINGING]

871
00:33:15,700 --> 00:33:19,570
-Shouldn't he be
 moving his lips?

872
00:33:19,570 --> 00:33:21,680
-No, I'm not gonna
 kill him right away.

873
00:33:21,680 --> 00:33:23,220
I'll let him linger.

874
00:33:23,220 --> 00:33:25,720
-[SINGING]

875
00:33:25,720 --> 00:33:31,980
-(SINGING) If I had
 a billion dollars.

876
00:33:31,980 --> 00:33:33,410
-They'd raise my taxes.

877
00:33:36,840 --> 00:33:39,860
-He makes Debbie Boone
 sound like Hound Dog Taylor.

878
00:33:42,730 --> 00:33:43,670
-I figured out.

879
00:33:43,670 --> 00:33:45,980
He's a cyst with teeth and hair.

880
00:33:45,980 --> 00:33:47,590
-(SINGING) To give to--

881
00:33:47,590 --> 00:33:50,970
-I demand you stop smiling.

882
00:33:50,970 --> 00:33:55,490
-Now, is she Billie Jo,
 Betty Jo, or Bobby Jo.

883
00:33:55,490 --> 00:33:56,390
-Please!
 Come on, Eegah!

884
00:33:56,390 --> 00:33:56,890
Hurry up!

885
00:33:56,890 --> 00:33:57,920
Where's that club?

886
00:33:57,920 --> 00:34:01,780
-(CHANTING) Eegah, Eegah,
 bonk bonk on the head.

887
00:34:04,570 --> 00:34:06,240
-(SINGING) Archie's here.

888
00:34:13,110 --> 00:34:14,270
-One way or the other.

889
00:34:14,270 --> 00:34:15,510
What do you think?

890
00:34:15,510 --> 00:34:16,390
-I don't know.

891
00:34:16,390 --> 00:34:17,610
-I've never thought before.

892
00:34:17,610 --> 00:34:18,780
-I'll climb up
 there a ways and see

893
00:34:18,780 --> 00:34:20,650
if the buggy can get through.

894
00:34:20,650 --> 00:34:21,670
-Or a shovel.

895
00:34:21,670 --> 00:34:23,000
Didn't ask to be in this movie.

896
00:34:23,000 --> 00:34:24,890
-No, you better stay here.

897
00:34:24,890 --> 00:34:25,800
-No!

898
00:34:25,800 --> 00:34:27,210
-There's no reason
 for both of us going.

899
00:34:27,210 --> 00:34:29,040
We gotta come back
 for the buggy anyway.

900
00:34:29,040 --> 00:34:30,140
-Well then we'll come back.

901
00:34:30,140 --> 00:34:32,150
I'm not going to sit
 here doing nothing.

902
00:34:32,150 --> 00:34:33,240
-Oh, women.

903
00:34:33,240 --> 00:34:33,970
-Let's see.

904
00:34:33,970 --> 00:34:35,170
What did I mean by that?

905
00:34:35,170 --> 00:34:36,640
-You stay here with the buggy.

906
00:34:36,640 --> 00:34:37,140
-Nope.

907
00:34:37,140 --> 00:34:39,220
-And drive it up to meet me
 when I give you the signal.

908
00:34:39,220 --> 00:34:40,830
That'll save us both a trip.

909
00:34:40,830 --> 00:34:42,030
Come on.

910
00:34:42,030 --> 00:34:42,690
-I'm whining you!

911
00:34:42,690 --> 00:34:43,660
Please!

912
00:34:43,660 --> 00:34:46,110
-Well, OK.

913
00:34:46,110 --> 00:34:46,790
-Aw, the gun.

914
00:34:46,790 --> 00:34:47,500
Toss it.

915
00:34:47,500 --> 00:34:48,340
-Now your lunch.

916
00:34:48,340 --> 00:34:50,230
Toss it.

917
00:34:50,230 --> 00:34:51,650
-Oh, I can see it coming.

918
00:34:51,650 --> 00:34:52,670
A tragic accident.

919
00:34:52,670 --> 00:34:53,860
Come on, come on-- aww.

920
00:34:53,860 --> 00:34:55,370
-Damn.

921
00:34:55,370 --> 00:34:57,760
-Give me a blast from that
 horn if you see anything.

922
00:34:57,760 --> 00:35:00,260
-Don't worry about that.

923
00:35:00,260 --> 00:35:02,870
-Oh, you know, he's built
 for child bearing, isn't he?

924
00:35:02,870 --> 00:35:03,370
-Serpentine!

925
00:35:03,370 --> 00:35:05,100
Serpentine!

926
00:35:05,100 --> 00:35:05,640
-I see a cactus!

927
00:35:05,640 --> 00:35:06,140
Honk!

928
00:35:06,140 --> 00:35:06,780
I see a lizard!

929
00:35:06,780 --> 00:35:07,280
Honk!

930
00:35:14,090 --> 00:35:15,320
-Keep going, you sap!

931
00:35:15,320 --> 00:35:16,340
Just over that ridge!

932
00:35:16,340 --> 00:35:17,040
That's it!

933
00:35:17,040 --> 00:35:18,390
I'm out of here.

934
00:35:21,060 --> 00:35:22,430
-Stay alive!

935
00:35:22,430 --> 00:35:24,740
Whatever may come,
 I will find you!

936
00:35:28,030 --> 00:35:28,530
-See?

937
00:35:28,530 --> 00:35:29,150
I told you so.

938
00:35:29,150 --> 00:35:30,410
Watch out for snakes.

939
00:35:33,660 --> 00:35:34,280
-Come on, boy.

940
00:35:34,280 --> 00:35:35,190
Just a little closer.

941
00:35:35,190 --> 00:35:36,430
Mm, smooth, pink meat.

942
00:35:36,430 --> 00:35:37,460
Wearing shorts, too.

943
00:35:37,460 --> 00:35:39,300
Mm, nothing but
 meat on that boy.

944
00:35:43,000 --> 00:35:47,390
-[HUMMING] Oh, I do want
 to look good for Eegah.

945
00:35:50,500 --> 00:35:53,110
-Why am I losing my
 hair in big chunks?

946
00:35:53,110 --> 00:35:56,200
-[HUMMING] Oh, nice
 steering wheel.

947
00:35:56,200 --> 00:35:57,300
I don't know about all this.

948
00:35:57,300 --> 00:35:58,070
It's sunny.

949
00:35:58,070 --> 00:36:00,020
My dress is blue.

950
00:36:00,020 --> 00:36:04,330
Oh, nice shovel. [HUMMING]
 What about my nose hairs?

951
00:36:04,330 --> 00:36:09,410
-You're here, and he's got
 the traveler's checks there.

952
00:36:09,410 --> 00:36:12,230
-Archie's in the Gaza Strip!

953
00:36:12,230 --> 00:36:15,160
-This is my country!

954
00:36:15,160 --> 00:36:16,750
-What was I looking for again?

955
00:36:16,750 --> 00:36:17,650
Sky?

956
00:36:17,650 --> 00:36:18,480
No, woman.

957
00:36:18,480 --> 00:36:20,110
I should have wrote
 that note to myself.

958
00:36:20,110 --> 00:36:21,530
It's weird the way it's so blue.

959
00:36:21,530 --> 00:36:22,610
Why are those buzzards circling?

960
00:36:22,610 --> 00:36:23,110
Huh.

961
00:36:23,110 --> 00:36:23,610
Neat.

962
00:36:30,530 --> 00:36:32,020
-(SINGING) Born free!

963
00:36:35,500 --> 00:36:37,000
-What-- what's that smell?

964
00:36:37,000 --> 00:36:38,440
Is that me?

965
00:36:38,440 --> 00:36:38,940
Oh.

966
00:36:38,940 --> 00:36:40,440
No?

967
00:36:40,440 --> 00:36:41,430
[HONK]

968
00:36:41,430 --> 00:36:42,430
-Don't hit!

969
00:36:45,420 --> 00:36:47,750
-Oh, he knows women, and she's
 going to want that purse.

970
00:36:47,750 --> 00:36:48,250
-Mm-hmm.

971
00:36:51,030 --> 00:36:54,220
-Uh, this-- this is really
 hard, finding the-- ow, caveman.

972
00:36:54,220 --> 00:36:55,030
Owie.

973
00:36:55,030 --> 00:36:55,760
-Oh, my girlish hips.

974
00:36:55,760 --> 00:36:56,260
Ow.

975
00:36:58,930 --> 00:36:59,670
-Huh?
 -Roxy!

976
00:36:59,670 --> 00:37:00,160
-Music!

977
00:37:00,160 --> 00:37:00,780
-Roxy!

978
00:37:00,780 --> 00:37:03,330
-And elsewhere!

979
00:37:03,330 --> 00:37:04,800
-Oh, I let another one.

980
00:37:04,800 --> 00:37:06,270
-Roxy!

981
00:37:06,270 --> 00:37:09,720
Roxy, where are you?

982
00:37:09,720 --> 00:37:11,670
-I'm being abducted!

983
00:37:11,670 --> 00:37:14,240
-You know, Eegah should
 have taken two trips.

984
00:37:14,240 --> 00:37:16,090
First the purse and the
 club, then the girl.

985
00:37:16,090 --> 00:37:17,420
Would've been easier.

986
00:37:20,160 --> 00:37:20,900
-Oh, boy.

987
00:37:20,900 --> 00:37:23,790
I made good time.

988
00:37:23,790 --> 00:37:24,520
-Oh no.

989
00:37:24,520 --> 00:37:27,220
He's got people stacked
 like cord wood in there!

990
00:37:31,510 --> 00:37:35,990
-He is this close to
 being Dom DeLuise.

991
00:37:35,990 --> 00:37:37,700
-Well, I see you've met Eegah.

992
00:37:37,700 --> 00:37:38,740
He'll spoil you.

993
00:37:38,740 --> 00:37:42,000
I'm spent.

994
00:37:42,000 --> 00:37:43,930
-Visit Cave of the
 Mounds, Dodgeville.

995
00:37:47,180 --> 00:37:48,160
-That's OK.

996
00:37:48,160 --> 00:37:51,140
Don't help.

997
00:37:51,140 --> 00:37:52,900
-[GROAN] Yep, yep.

998
00:37:52,900 --> 00:37:56,120
This looks much better over
 here by the lime deposit.

999
00:37:56,120 --> 00:37:57,120
-Eegah, I woke up.

1000
00:37:57,120 --> 00:37:57,700
You weren't here.

1001
00:37:57,700 --> 00:37:58,390
I hate that.

1002
00:38:03,750 --> 00:38:09,600
-[HUMMING]

1003
00:38:09,600 --> 00:38:11,640
-Eegah, you said
 you lived alone!

1004
00:38:11,640 --> 00:38:12,770
-[GRUNTING "HERE
 COMES THE BRIDE"]

1005
00:38:16,710 --> 00:38:17,210
-There.

1006
00:38:17,210 --> 00:38:17,710
Play nice.

1007
00:38:20,740 --> 00:38:21,320
-Roxy.

1008
00:38:21,320 --> 00:38:24,010
You finally break up with
 that weird faced kid?

1009
00:38:24,010 --> 00:38:25,480
-Roxy.

1010
00:38:25,480 --> 00:38:27,440
-[GRUNTING]

1011
00:38:27,440 --> 00:38:28,060
-I got it.

1012
00:38:28,060 --> 00:38:28,640
Don't worry.

1013
00:38:28,640 --> 00:38:29,140
-Roxy?

1014
00:38:29,140 --> 00:38:29,950
-Oopie.

1015
00:38:29,950 --> 00:38:30,450
-Roxy!

1016
00:38:30,450 --> 00:38:30,950
-Dad!

1017
00:38:30,950 --> 00:38:31,480
-Wow.

1018
00:38:31,480 --> 00:38:33,410
She can snap in and out of
 consciousness, can't she?

1019
00:38:33,410 --> 00:38:34,740
-Oh, dad.

1020
00:38:34,740 --> 00:38:35,620
-Oh.

1021
00:38:35,620 --> 00:38:37,450
-Oh, are you hurt?

1022
00:38:37,450 --> 00:38:39,930
-No, I wear this thing
 for effect, you doorknob.

1023
00:38:39,930 --> 00:38:40,430
-Here.

1024
00:38:40,430 --> 00:38:41,520
Let me help you.

1025
00:38:41,520 --> 00:38:42,020
-Ow!

1026
00:38:42,020 --> 00:38:42,940
That's OK.

1027
00:38:42,940 --> 00:38:44,650
-How did you get here?

1028
00:38:44,650 --> 00:38:47,400
-Well, we came looking
 for you, and-- and we

1029
00:38:47,400 --> 00:38:50,480
were both so worried that
 we didn't know what to do.

1030
00:38:50,480 --> 00:38:51,480
-No, no.

1031
00:38:51,480 --> 00:38:52,930
No.

1032
00:38:52,930 --> 00:38:53,860
No, no.

1033
00:38:53,860 --> 00:38:55,310
-No, just the check.

1034
00:38:55,310 --> 00:38:56,050
-No, no.

1035
00:38:56,050 --> 00:38:57,400
She is mine.

1036
00:38:57,400 --> 00:39:01,770
-(SINGING) The
 doggone girl is mine.

1037
00:39:01,770 --> 00:39:04,260
-She's mine.

1038
00:39:04,260 --> 00:39:06,750
-He understands you.

1039
00:39:06,750 --> 00:39:09,770
-Oh, we've got a beautiful
 friendship going.

1040
00:39:09,770 --> 00:39:12,030
-Is that irony, dad?

1041
00:39:12,030 --> 00:39:14,920
-[SPEAKING_CAVEMAN]

1042
00:39:14,920 --> 00:39:15,740
-What's he saying?

1043
00:39:15,740 --> 00:39:18,930
Shimmy shimmy cocoa pop?

1044
00:39:18,930 --> 00:39:20,180
-Take it easy.

1045
00:39:20,180 --> 00:39:20,680
-Dad!

1046
00:39:20,680 --> 00:39:21,210
-Oh, no.

1047
00:39:21,210 --> 00:39:25,240
This guy went to the
 Torgo School of Fondling.

1048
00:39:25,240 --> 00:39:25,740
-Me?

1049
00:39:25,740 --> 00:39:26,990
Scare him?

1050
00:39:26,990 --> 00:39:27,490
-Smile.

1051
00:39:27,490 --> 00:39:29,860
-Mm, smell Love's Baby Soft.

1052
00:39:32,460 --> 00:39:33,780
-Now you smell him, honey.

1053
00:39:33,780 --> 00:39:35,570
[SNIFFING]

1054
00:39:35,570 --> 00:39:39,050
-Scent of a Woman.

1055
00:39:39,050 --> 00:39:41,460
-He likes your perfume.

1056
00:39:41,460 --> 00:39:42,930
-Smell all you want.

1057
00:39:42,930 --> 00:39:44,760
-But take all you smell.

1058
00:39:44,760 --> 00:39:46,630
-What became of the others?

1059
00:39:46,630 --> 00:39:48,030
-What others?

1060
00:39:48,030 --> 00:39:48,960
-Keep smiling.

1061
00:39:48,960 --> 00:39:51,510
You didn't come out
 here alone, did you?

1062
00:39:51,510 --> 00:39:52,160
-No.

1063
00:39:52,160 --> 00:39:52,910
-Tish, that's French.

1064
00:39:52,910 --> 00:39:53,740
-Tom's with me.

1065
00:39:53,740 --> 00:39:56,170
I mean, he's out
 there someplace.

1066
00:39:56,170 --> 00:39:57,140
-Oh.

1067
00:39:57,140 --> 00:39:58,050
He's just curious.

1068
00:39:58,050 --> 00:39:58,650
Hold still.

1069
00:39:58,650 --> 00:40:00,080
-Aw, he's pawing me, daddy.

1070
00:40:00,080 --> 00:40:02,760
-That's OK, precious.

1071
00:40:02,760 --> 00:40:05,190
-Eegah like get caught in rain.

1072
00:40:05,190 --> 00:40:08,820
-It's real, see?

1073
