2183
01:19:56,610 --> 01:19:58,680
Dad, I've got the
 funniest feeling.

2184
01:19:58,680 --> 01:19:59,700
-Downstairs.

2185
01:19:59,700 --> 01:20:01,010
-What is it?

2186
01:20:01,010 --> 01:20:02,810
-You know, stuff.

2187
01:20:02,810 --> 01:20:03,910
-I can't describe it.

2188
01:20:03,910 --> 01:20:06,970
But I just know something's
 happened to him.

2189
01:20:06,970 --> 01:20:08,270
-Him?

2190
01:20:08,270 --> 01:20:08,960
-Eegah.

2191
01:20:08,960 --> 01:20:09,690
-Who's Eegah?

2192
01:20:09,690 --> 01:20:10,370
-The giant.

2193
01:20:10,370 --> 01:20:11,230
-Oh, yeah.

2194
01:20:11,230 --> 01:20:14,340
-Or whatever he is.

2195
01:20:14,340 --> 01:20:16,050
Something's happened to him.

2196
01:20:16,050 --> 01:20:18,390
-Roxy, look at me.

2197
01:20:18,390 --> 01:20:19,540
I love you very much.

2198
01:20:19,540 --> 01:20:22,440
-I wish I could
 return the sentiment.

2199
01:20:22,440 --> 01:20:24,660
-Every living thing was
 her personal concern,

2200
01:20:24,660 --> 01:20:28,040
and she worried about them.

2201
01:20:28,040 --> 01:20:30,650
-I gotta go tan now.

2202
01:20:30,650 --> 01:20:32,000
-That's just it, dad.

2203
01:20:32,000 --> 01:20:36,520
But you see, worry isn't
 the feeling that I have.

2204
01:20:36,520 --> 01:20:38,380
-It's more nausea.

2205
01:20:38,380 --> 01:20:39,610
-I don't know what it is.

2206
01:20:39,610 --> 01:20:41,390
He's a creature.

2207
01:20:41,390 --> 01:20:44,550
Why, you just have to
 look at him to see that.

2208
01:20:44,550 --> 01:20:46,110
He even tried to kill us.

2209
01:20:46,110 --> 01:20:48,330
-But basically, he's a good egg.

2210
01:20:48,330 --> 01:20:50,360
-But just--

2211
01:20:50,360 --> 01:20:52,960
-You can't get him
 out of your mind.

2212
01:20:52,960 --> 01:20:54,880
-Bonk!

2213
01:20:54,880 --> 01:20:58,900
-Is this is "The Third
 Man" all of a sudden?

2214
01:20:58,900 --> 01:21:00,200
-Oh, Eegah's a mall walker.

2215
01:21:03,840 --> 01:21:05,900
-[GRUMBLING] Oh, that's cheap.

2216
01:21:05,900 --> 01:21:06,910
But I gotta go now.

2217
01:21:06,910 --> 01:21:07,940
-You can always go back for it.

2218
01:21:07,940 --> 01:21:10,530
-That's my job for
 about two more years.

2219
01:21:10,530 --> 01:21:12,570
If I can hold onto
 you that long.

2220
01:21:12,570 --> 01:21:14,460
Then it'll be up
 to somebody else.

2221
01:21:14,460 --> 01:21:17,400
-Hey, Richard Speck is there.

2222
01:21:17,400 --> 01:21:18,570
-Maybe him, huh?

2223
01:21:18,570 --> 01:21:20,710
-No!

2224
01:21:20,710 --> 01:21:21,760
-Hey.

2225
01:21:21,760 --> 01:21:23,740
Where you been?

2226
01:21:23,740 --> 01:21:26,140
I was belting out a tune
 just for you in there.

2227
01:21:26,140 --> 01:21:27,460
I look up, and you're gone.

2228
01:21:27,460 --> 01:21:28,770
-We could hear every word, Tom.

2229
01:21:28,770 --> 01:21:30,540
I said hear, not understand.

2230
01:21:30,540 --> 01:21:31,770
[SIRENS]

2231
01:21:31,770 --> 01:21:33,450
-You're funny, Mr. Miller.

2232
01:21:33,450 --> 01:21:34,730
Really funny.

2233
01:21:34,730 --> 01:21:35,750
-I'm being sarcastic.

2234
01:21:35,750 --> 01:21:36,540
-Come on, Roxy.

2235
01:21:36,540 --> 01:21:37,070
Let's dance.

2236
01:21:37,070 --> 01:21:37,570
-Wait a minute.

2237
01:21:37,570 --> 01:21:39,740
-What's the matter?

2238
01:21:39,740 --> 01:21:41,290
-I thought I heard sirens.

2239
